# 20. Recreating the Ingress

We recreated the Ingress.

The important change was to remove the hostname restriction.

Instead of:

```yaml
rules:
- host: html.local
```

we used:

```yaml
rules:
- http:
    paths:
    - path: /
      pathType: Prefix
      backend:
        service:
          name: html-service
          port:
            number: 80
```

Now:

```bash
kubectl get ingress
```

returned:

```text
NAME           CLASS   HOSTS   ADDRESS   PORTS
html-ingress   nginx   *                 80
```

The critical value is:

```text
HOSTS *
```

This means the Ingress accepts requests regardless of the HTTP Host header.

